    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "04ef883c_be74130f",
        "filename": "media/libaudiohal/impl/DeviceHalAidl.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 117,
      "author": {
        "id": 1042638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-19T17:25:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is `instance:` in the log macros:\n\n```\n...[instance:%s] ...\", getInstanceName().c_str()\n```\n\nWe need to remove either of these. From the fact that we intend to use `ioHandle:` prefix for streams, I think we need to remove the prefix from the log macros, for example:\n\n```\n#define LOG_ENTRY() \\\n    ALOGD(\"[%s] %s::%s\", getInstanceName().c_str(), getClassName().c_str(), __func__)\n```",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 117,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 117,
        "endChar": 66
      },
      "revId": "72c87f047d7a5faf89b59e1b089c14eb17650987",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8c63ef1b_331b6f21",
        "filename": "media/libaudiohal/impl/DeviceHalAidl.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 9
      },
      "lineNbr": 187,
      "author": {
        "id": 1956242
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-19T22:05:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If we define `LOG_ENTRY` to accept arguments, then all `DeviceHalAidl` `StreamHalAidl` methods can either start with `LOG_ENTRY()`, or in this case where we want additional information it will be `LOG_ENTRY(\"volume %f\", volume)`",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 187,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 187,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "72c87f047d7a5faf89b59e1b089c14eb17650987",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
